  "id": "COMPOUND:3962 - PROTEIN:6000",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Dequalinium may interact with Lysosomal phospholipase A2 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway involves Dequalinium as a target of 1-Hydroxy-3-[4-(3-Methylbut-2-Enoxy)Phenyl]-4-(2-Methylpropyl)Pyrrole-2,5-Dione, which in turn targets Lysosomal phospholipase A2. The second pathway links Dequalinium to UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B15, which is targeted by Aeruginosin DA722, and this enzyme also targets Lysosomal phospholipase A2. Both pathways indicate a potential mechanism by which Dequalinium could influence Lysosomal phospholipase A2 activity, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The scores from the two paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of Dequalinium in this process.",
